r">359 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Philip II becomes king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and begins reforming its army</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">338 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Philip defeats <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce">Chaeronea</a> and becomes master of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">334 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Alexander crosses into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and wins his first victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-granicus">Granicus</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">331 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Alexander defeats Darius III at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a>, sealing the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">326 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Alexander defeats <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hydaspes">Hydaspes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">323 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Alexander dies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, leaving no clear successor</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">168 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> defeats the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonid-dynasty">Antigonid</a> king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pydna">Pydna</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">146 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Macedonia becomes a Roman province, ending independent Macedonian rule</span></li></ol>
